nodecode-0bull is a rewrite of 0bull's 0bull/agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/0bull/agent-plugin
  commit 240890a71715375bc877b238491e414517e9d902
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 NANIMAD SL (0bull) (LICENSE)

The plugin was a portable Agent Plugins v1 package with no code of its own:
plugin.json, mcp.json declaring the hosted MCP server at https://0bull.net/mcp
(Streamable HTTP, OAuth), and three skills, 0bull-iphone-control,
0bull-tiktok-post and 0bull-youtube-post, that taught a model the workflow.
This rewrite speaks that server's MCP wire itself, in Common Lisp over
nlk:http -- initialize, the Mcp-Session-Id, one JSON-RPC POST per call, an
answer that is either a JSON object or a one-event stream -- and keeps the
server's own tool names (list-phones-tool, phone-control-tool,
create-submission-tool and the rest) behind seven purpose-named tools. The
three skills' rules, the statuses they listed and the things they said never
to do are the cell's manual topic, (help :0bull), and its one-line summary
in every request. What was left out: plugin.json and mcp.json as manifests,
which the cell contract replaces with a section and a declaration; the OAuth
browser flow, which the shipped mcp cell already owns, so this cell reuses
that sign-in or a pasted token; create-upload-url-tool, so a video arrives as
a public url or an upload_id; and the server's rental and billing tools,
which spend money, so the model cannot call them by accident. Nothing of the
original is vendored: there was no code to vendor.
